                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "1143acc2-3aa4-4044-9867-c9c944f4391e",
                        "entry_id": "e97b2e5e-7ab7-328c-8a82-ea9dc2049287",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "гренла́ндских"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4ad61337-2739-3058-93db-9c6a26246aa8",
                        "entry_id": "e97b2e5e-7ab7-328c-8a82-ea9dc2049287",
                        "glosses": [
                            "относящийся к Гренландии, гренландцам"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8c35e1d0-92e8-4e76-971e-f2b7717eddad",
                                "sense_id": "4ad61337-2739-3058-93db-9c6a26246aa8",
                                "text": "Наш северо-запад, изобилующий громадными стадами гренландского тюленя, не особенно нуждается в морже, как побережья, указанные выше."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "40d1944d-acf0-4396-8011-28786968e1f1",
                                "sense_id": "4ad61337-2739-3058-93db-9c6a26246aa8",
                                "text": "К беззубым относятся полосатики, синие, гренландские киты, горбачи и другие."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "be654814-9bf0-4b0a-855b-1be3b5286283",
                                "sense_id": "4ad61337-2739-3058-93db-9c6a26246aa8",
                                "text": "Исследователи величайшего из островов земного шара Гренландии утверждают, что он покрыт слоем льда огромной толщины, доходящей в центральных частях до 2700 м; средняя же толщина гренландского ледника принимается равной 1600 м."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "758599b0-e3ff-4314-a348-19691d2f96fb",
                                "sense_id": "4ad61337-2739-3058-93db-9c6a26246aa8",
                                "text": "В гренландских поселениях скандинавских колонистов найдены остатки примерно трехсот хуторов, двух монастырей и многочисленных церквей."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "495ac661-dab5-4af6-bee9-3e3428786c11",
                                "sense_id": "4ad61337-2739-3058-93db-9c6a26246aa8",
                                "text": "Так чума приехала в Скандинавию. Здесь она выкосила четверть населения, в том числе и последних викингов, что жили в глухих деревушках на гренландских фьордах."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2dcc73e3-e41d-34cf-98a1-29398bac6300",
                        "entry_id": "e97b2e5e-7ab7-328c-8a82-ea9dc2049287",
                        "glosses": [
                            "субстантивир. то же, что гренландский язык; язык эскимосов Гренландии, относящийся к группе инуит эскимосско-алеутской семьи"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cfd37c59-8399-485d-9d33-f87018ad29d6",
                        "source_entry_id": "e97b2e5e-7ab7-328c-8a82-ea9dc2049287",
                        "target_lang_word": "Greenlandish",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Greenlandish",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ca2dceef-5f0a-3e0b-808b-e9fc9722087e",
                                        "entry_id": "f125d7e1-3e1e-32d2-9e23-332276e4ba21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dated form of Greenlandic (“pertaining to Greenland”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "dated",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "536fbc48-2719-4f96-a6d8-20607c4cb7d8",
                                                "sense_id": "ca2dceef-5f0a-3e0b-808b-e9fc9722087e",
                                                "text": "Intimately connected with the question of the date is that of the home of Eddic poetry. There is fair agreement about only two poems: \"Atlamál,\" which is generally allowed to be of Greenlandish origin, and the \"Prophecy of Grípir,\" which no doubt was composed by an Icelander of the twelfth century […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Greenlandish",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "05c020f6-caea-3f19-be0c-70677488f01c",
                                        "entry_id": "dd26f4e5-624b-3544-b9ef-45f14356c797",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dated form of Greenlandic (“language of Greenland”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc85b72b-83ee-4786-8277-065c8fc05c5a",
                                                "sense_id": "05c020f6-caea-3f19-be0c-70677488f01c",
                                                "text": "Taking it for granted that Greenlandish may be held to represent the Eskimo tongue in general, we shall endeavour to give an idea of its remarkable construction."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f600494f-31ed-41bf-ac18-1d05a3b0b6a4",
                                                "sense_id": "05c020f6-caea-3f19-be0c-70677488f01c",
                                                "text": "The linguistic character of Faroese and Greenlandish are very different, Greenlandish being an Eskimo language whereas Faroese is a Nordic language with roots in Old Norwegian."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ceee8ac2-0222-47df-933c-6626eb5ead80",
                        "source_entry_id": "e97b2e5e-7ab7-328c-8a82-ea9dc2049287",
                        "target_lang_word": "Greenlandic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Greenlandic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7f1cee6b-47ef-3337-8b22-e14788e50a1f",
                                        "entry_id": "77c767b6-5874-362f-be07-6909501b29f3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of, from, or pertaining to Greenland, the Greenlandic people or the Greenlandic language."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a553bb29-d845-4d77-9490-b9f6b9c664d1",
                                                "sense_id": "7f1cee6b-47ef-3337-8b22-e14788e50a1f",
                                                "text": "In 2014, the Greenlandic government — called the Naalakkersuisut — established a reconciliation commission to investigate the continuing consequences of colonialism. After three years, the commission concluded that a majority of the nearly 60,000 people living in Greenland, 88 percent of whom are Greenlandic Inuit, are still marked by the negative effects of the colonial period."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Greenlandic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ad9348ed-a312-3ff7-bbe2-40faca2b5846",
                                        "entry_id": "276cf5f9-526d-3748-917a-c3983533a2b0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The official language of Greenland, an Eskimo-Aleut language written with the Latin alphabet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "415c86da-307e-49c5-9bbc-91e672133abe",
                                                "sense_id": "ad9348ed-a312-3ff7-bbe2-40faca2b5846",
                                                "text": "Nevertheless, it may be too late—mistakes in Greenlandic already seem to have become embedded in machine translators. If you prompt either Google Translate or ChatGPT to do something as simple as count to 10 in proper Greenlandic, neither program can deliver."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2e50c34e-ec58-475f-b141-4fa787b1b26f",
                        "source_entry_id": "e97b2e5e-7ab7-328c-8a82-ea9dc2049287",
